  "notes": "This is the original US release with custom labels, and custom group logo inner sleeve with illustration.\n\n[l408779] pressing variant as indicated by \"PR\" etching in the run-outs.\n\nThe text layout on the labels may be slightly different from other similar versions. No label matrix printed on labels of this version.\n\nFirst catalog number on cover and labels, second catalog number on inner sleeve.\n\n℗ © 1973 Phonogram Inc.\n\nAll selections published by Lipstick Killers Pub., Inc.(ASCAP), except \"Pills\" published by Arc Music Corp. (BMI)\n\nThis album is dedicated to Billy Doll\n\nAlso available on Musicassette and Stereo 8 Tapes MCR-4-1-675 - MC-8-1-675\n\nSome copies include Phonogram Inc. company postcard mailer insert with catalog request form from the Mercury Family of Labels.\n\nRunouts are etched, STERLING stamped.",
  "released_formatted": "1973",
